2186076262 1078 #edb/ref 17592186444204 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186077828 1078 #edb/ref 17592186077829 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078158 1071 "List all terms of the expression $3x + 2y - 4x$." 13194139534921 17592186045417 false] [17592186078158 1071 "List all terms of the expression $3x + 2y - 4x.$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078158 1074 "We put an addition symbol $(+)$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(3x) + (2y) + (-4x)\n$$\n\nSo, the expression has three terms: $3x$, $2y$, and $-4x.$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078158 1074 "We put an addition symbol $(+)$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$(3x) + (2y) + (-4x)$\nSo, the expression has three terms: $3x$, $2y$, and $-4x$." 13194139534921 17592186045417 false] [17592186078159 1071 "What is the fourth term of the expression $2t + 5s - \\dfrac{1}{2}s + 8t$?" 13194139534921 17592186045417 false] [17592186078159 1071 "What is the fourth term of the expression $2t + 5s - \\dfrac{1}{2}s + 8t?$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078159 1074 "We put an addition symbol $(+)$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(2t) + (5s) + \\left( -\\dfrac{1}{2} s \\right) + (8t)\n$$\n\nCounting off the terms:\n\n- the first term is $2t,$\n\n- the second term is $5s,$\n\n- the third term is $-\\dfrac{1}{2}s,$ and\n\n- the fourth term is $8t.$\n\nIn particular, we are interested in the fourth term. The fourth term is $8t.$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078159 1074 "We put an addition symbol $(+)$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(2t) + (5s) + \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{2} s \\right) + (8t)\n$$\n\nCounting off the terms:\n\n- the first term is $2t$,\n- the second term is $5s$,\n- the third term is $-\\dfrac{1}{2}s$, and\n- the fourth term is $8t$.\n\nIn particular, we are interested in the fourth term. The fourth term is $8t$." 13194139534921 17592186045417 false] [17592186078160 1071 "Write down an expression that is equivalent to $9-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+3y$." 13194139534921 17592186045417 false] [17592186078160 1071 "Write down an expression that is equivalent to $9-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+3y.$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078160 1074 "The expression\n\n$$\n9-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+3y\n$$\n\nhas three terms: $9$,\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{1}{2}x\n$$\n\nand $3y$.\n\nIt doesn't matter in what order we write the terms. For example, one equivalent expression is:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{1}{2}x + 3y +9\n$$\n\nAnother equivalent expression is:\n\n$$\n3y - \\dfrac{1}{2}x + 9\n$$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 false] [17592186078160 1074 "The expression $9-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+3y$ has three terms: $9,$ $-\\dfrac{1}{2}x,$ and $3y.$\n\nIt doesn't matter in what order we write the terms. For example, one equivalent expression is:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{1}{2}x + 3y +9\n$$\n\nAnother equivalent expression is:\n\n$$\n3y - \\dfrac{1}{2}x + 9\n$$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078613 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444245 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078613 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444248 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078613 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444251 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078613 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444254 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078613 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444255 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078614 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444246 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078614 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444249 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078614 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444250 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078614 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444252 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078615 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444247 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078615 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444253 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078615 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444256 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078665 1050 420.0 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078756 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078756 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to the expression $\\frac{1}{3}b + 2a$?" 13194139534921 17592186045417 false] [17592186078756 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to the expression $\\frac{1}{3}b+2a?$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078756 1074 "The expression $\\frac{1}{3}b+2a$ has two terms: $\\frac{1}{3}b$ and $2a.$ \n\nThe order in which we combine the terms doesn't matter. Therefore, we can also write this expression as \n\n$$\n2a+\\frac{1}{3}b.\n$$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078914 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078914 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to the expression $6z + \\frac{3}{2}x + 2y + \\frac{5}{2}$?" 13194139534921 17592186045417 false] [17592186078914 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to the expression $6z+\\frac{3}{2}x+2y+\\frac{5}{2}?$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186078914 1074 "The expression $6z+\\frac{3}{2}x+2y+\\frac{5}{2}$ has four terms:  $6z$, $\\frac{3}{2}x$, $2y$ and $\\frac{5}{2}.$ \n\nThe order in which we combine the terms doesn't matter. Therefore, we can also write this expression as \n\n$$\n2y+\\frac{5}{2}+6z+\\frac{3}{2}x.\n$$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186079175 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186079175 1071 "What is the fourth term of the expression $5a - \\frac{4}{3}b - 12c + \\frac{1}{2}d$?" 13194139534921 17592186045417 false] [17592186079175 1071 "What is the fourth term of the expression $5a-\\frac{4}{3}b-12c+\\frac{1}{2}d?$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186079175 1074 "We put an addition symbol $(+)$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(5a)+(-\\frac{4}{3}b)+(-12c)+(\\frac{1}{2}d)\n$$\n\nCounting off the terms:\n\n- the first term is $5a,$\n\n- the second term is $-\\frac{4}{3}b,$\n\n- the third term is $-12c,$ and\n\n- the fourth term is $\\frac{1}{2}d.$\n\nIn particular, we are interested in the fourth term. The fourth term is $\\frac{1}{2}d.$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186079714 1064 "Let's take a look at the following algebraic expression:\n\n$$\n2x{\\,\\color{red}{-}\\,} 4y {\\,\\color{blue}{+}\\,} 7\n$$\n\nThe addition $({\\color{blue}{+}})$ and subtraction $({\\color{red}{-}})$ symbols separate this expression into three parts known as **terms**.  \n\nTo identify each term, we put an addition symbol $({\\color{blue}{+}})$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(2x) {\\,\\color{blue}{+}\\,} ({\\,\\color{red}{-}\\,} 4y) {\\,\\color{blue}{+}\\,} (7).\n$$\n\nSo, the terms of this expression are: \n\n$$\n2x,\\quad -4y,\\quad  \\quad 7\n$$\n\nWe say that $2x$ is the **first term**, $-4y$ is the **second term**, and $7$ is the **third term**. \n\nIn this example, the subtraction symbol gave us the term $-4y$. Whenever there is a subtraction symbol, the corresponding term will be negative." 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186079714 1064 "Let's take a look at the following algebraic expression:\n$2x{\\,\\color{red}{-}\\,} 4y {\\,\\color{blue}{+}\\,} 7$\nThe addition $({\\color{blue}{+}})$ and subtraction $({\\color{red}{-}})$ symbols separate this expression into three parts known as **terms**.\n\nTo identify each term, we put an addition symbol $({\\color{blue}{+}})$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(2x) {\\,\\color{blue}{+}\\,} ({\\,\\color{red}{-}\\,} 4y) {\\,\\color{blue}{+}\\,} (7)\n$$\n\nSo, the terms of this expression are:\n$2x,\\quad -4y,\\quad \\quad 7$\nWe say that $2x$ is the **first term**, $-4y$ is the **second term**, and $7$ is the **third term**.\n\nIn this example, the subtraction symbol gave us the term $-4y$. Whenever there is a subtraction symbol, the corresponding term will be negative." 13194139534921 17592186045417 false] [17592186079715 1064 "When two algebraic expressions contain exactly the same terms, they are said to be **equivalent**.\n\nFor example, the expression\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{2y}} + 3z\n$$\n\nis equivalent to \n\n$$\n3z+{\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{2y}}\n$$\n\nbecause they both contain the exact same terms. Both expressions are also equivalent to\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{x}} + 3z+ {\\color{red}{2y}}.\n$$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186079715 1064 "When two algebraic expressions contain exactly the same terms, they are said to be **equivalent**.\n\nFor example, the expression\n${\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{2y}} + 3z$\nis equivalent to\n$3z+{\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{2y}}$\nbecause they both contain the exact same terms. Both expressions are also equivalent to\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{x}} + 3z+ {\\color{red}{2y}}\n$$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 false] [17592186444175 1080 "xyz" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186444175 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186444175 1083 #uuid "029b656c-ed51-5555-9c8d-27587222dae8" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186444176 1080 "$2d$, $-9e$, and $5f$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186444176 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186444176 1083 #uuid "03cd6056-ba55-56db-84a2-95b8cbd254de" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186444177 1080 "$p$, $2q$, and $3r$" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186444177 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186444177 1083 #uuid "0a763403-d8be-5f61-a2b2-6ad454e7dff4" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186444178 1080 "-\\frac{4}{5}b" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186444178 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186444178 1083 #uuid "0b22e6da-e6a8-537b-8f51-6e282c9f5b0f" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186444179 1080 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534921 17592186045417 true] [17592186444179 1082 #edb/ref 1759